@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Approvals & Gates in Azure Pipelines";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Approvals and Gates in Azure DevOps Pipelines provide **controlled deployment workflows**, ensuring that changes are reviewed and meet required conditions before proceeding to the next stage.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>What Are Approvals & Gates?</h2>
        <p>Approvals and Gates allow organizations to enforce **deployment control** by adding validation steps in the pipeline.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>**Approvals** – Require manual intervention before a deployment proceeds.</li>
            <li>**Gates** – Perform automated checks (e.g., security scans, monitoring) before approving a release.</li>
            <li>**Ensures compliance** and reduces risk in production deployments.</li>
            <li>Prevents deployments from proceeding until conditions are met.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/approvals-gates.png" alt="Approvals & Gates in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Approvals & Gates in a Release Pipeline</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Types of Approvals</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>**Pre-Deployment Approvals** – Approvers must manually approve before moving to the next stage.</li>
                <li>**Post-Deployment Approvals** – Approval is required after deployment to ensure system stability.</li>
                <li>**Multi-User Approvals** – Multiple users or teams must review before proceeding.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Configuring Approvals in Azure DevOps</h2>
        <p>Follow these steps to set up Approvals in a Release Pipeline:</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Go to **Azure DevOps > Pipelines > Releases**.</li>
            <li>Select a stage and click **Pre-deployment conditions**.</li>
            <li>Enable **Pre-deployment approvals** and specify approvers.</li>
            <li>Save and deploy the pipeline.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>What Are Gates in Azure Pipelines?</h2>
        <p>Gates are **automated checks** that must be satisfied before a deployment continues.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Checks **system health, security policies, and compliance**.</li>
            <li>Can be configured with **Azure Monitor alerts, REST API calls, and security scans**.</li>
            <li>Ensures **data-driven decision-making** before deployments.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Example YAML for Approval & Gates</h4>
            <pre>
stages:
- stage: Deploy
  displayName: 'Deploy with Approval'
  jobs:
  - deployment: DeployWebApp
    environment: 'Production'
    strategy:
      runOnce:
        deploy:
          steps:
          - task: AzureWebApp@1
            inputs:
              azureSubscription: 'AzureServiceConnection'
              appName: 'my-web-app'
              package: '$(Pipeline.Workspace)/drop/*.zip'
            </pre>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/gates-example.png" alt="Example of Gates in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Example of Gates in a Pipeline</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Best Practices for Approvals & Gates</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Use **pre-deployment approvals** for controlled rollouts.</li>
            <li>Automate security and compliance checks with **Gates**.</li>
            <li>Enable **multi-stage approvals** for high-risk deployments.</li>
            <li>Monitor deployment **logs and alerts** to track approval decisions.</li>
            <li>Use **role-based access control (RBAC)** to define approvers.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Approvals & Gates in Azure DevOps Pipelines enforce **deployment control, compliance, and automated checks**. By integrating approvals and gates, organizations can ensure **secure, stable, and reliable software releases**.
        </p>
        <p>
            The next step is to explore **Rollback Strategies in Azure DevOps** for handling failed deployments effectively.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("DeployAzureAppServices", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: Deploying to Azure App Services</a>
        <a href="@Url.Action("RollbackStrategies", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next: Rollback Strategies &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>
